[{:db/id 17592186059860 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6797302b-db97-5343-8bcd-03d0be79c3e6" "question-3ba307ad-392e-5e93-b33f-bf270e666d44" "question-b33a7a36-0a25-50da-8f78-4cfda2b51bbb" "question-d83cabb0-45f8-5769-8a35-16968ddc61ef"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059420 :question/worked-solution "The red arrow indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values greater than $2.$ In addition, the filled red circle at $2$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $2.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents the numbers that are greater than or equal to $2.$ This corresponds the inequality $x \\geq 2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059421 :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$<$\" means \"less than.\"  So, the inequality $x < -1$ represents the numbers that are less than $-1.$\n\nOn a number line, the numbers less than $-1$ are the numbers that are left of  $-1.$ So, we should draw an arrow going to the left of $-1.$\n\nHowever, the number $-1$ itself is not less than $-1,$ so we should not include it in our representation. To exclude $-1,$ we draw an empty circle around $-1.$\n\n![](images/57/57499770d310c5f0912e62ec160accd878a1c169c22ce894a48102a39769d209.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-6797302b-db97-5343-8bcd-03d0be79c3e6" :question/id #uuid "6797302b-db97-5343-8bcd-03d0be79c3e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-180943" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f20c29602002cfc9310e69da692096f11eede3602f481ed23199fecefdc67ec6.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "There is a **closed** circle at $x=-\\frac{3}{2},$ and the red arrow starts from $-\\frac{3}{2}$ and goes to the **left**. This indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **less than or equal** to $-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x\\le -\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dff4734c-e402-5cf1-b36f-6fdafdb2be9f" "answer-field-2839a5ea-d1c6-5bba-aa69-40c780d7f1aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dff4734c-e402-5cf1-b36f-6fdafdb2be9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "dff4734c-e402-5cf1-b36f-6fdafdb2be9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a676959d-6ea0-5065-98f5-5e572da516c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a676959d-6ea0-5065-98f5-5e572da516c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a676959d-6ea0-5065-98f5-5e572da516c7" :answer/id #uuid "a676959d-6ea0-5065-98f5-5e572da516c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2839a5ea-d1c6-5bba-aa69-40c780d7f1aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "2839a5ea-d1c6-5bba-aa69-40c780d7f1aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c032b333-6e7d-5a0a-9633-7aa7f47efab2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c032b333-6e7d-5a0a-9633-7aa7f47efab2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c032b333-6e7d-5a0a-9633-7aa7f47efab2" :answer/id #uuid "c032b333-6e7d-5a0a-9633-7aa7f47efab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ba307ad-392e-5e93-b33f-bf270e666d44" :question/id #uuid "3ba307ad-392e-5e93-b33f-bf270e666d44" :question/math-academy-id "q-180941" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa66ca8b5322c540313074b2a54c72651994967865bd99b1f1fa7d8f3b44c7a8.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "There is a **closed** circle at $x=2,$ and the red arrow starts from $2$ and goes to the **left**. This indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **less than or equal** to $2.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x\\le 2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ec5d004-f525-5d66-ad93-04b9f0bf94e7" "answer-field-d3156f84-5b12-5fa2-b680-693ae024585b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ec5d004-f525-5d66-ad93-04b9f0bf94e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec5d004-f525-5d66-ad93-04b9f0bf94e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d9b745d8-f42a-5123-b3b4-f4961fa0bdbb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9b745d8-f42a-5123-b3b4-f4961fa0bdbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9b745d8-f42a-5123-b3b4-f4961fa0bdbb" :answer/id #uuid "d9b745d8-f42a-5123-b3b4-f4961fa0bdbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3156f84-5b12-5fa2-b680-693ae024585b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3156f84-5b12-5fa2-b680-693ae024585b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c1df1ed6-61e0-5f5e-a6ca-bbdfde940fc0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1df1ed6-61e0-5f5e-a6ca-bbdfde940fc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1df1ed6-61e0-5f5e-a6ca-bbdfde940fc0" :answer/id #uuid "c1df1ed6-61e0-5f5e-a6ca-bbdfde940fc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b33a7a36-0a25-50da-8f78-4cfda2b51bbb" :question/id #uuid "b33a7a36-0a25-50da-8f78-4cfda2b51bbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-54757" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2fc316ce27f19d738daf33ba7f3efa5109f4489f9c63ed2c2c40c4c66e9388cf.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "There is an **open** circle at $x=-2,$ and the red arrow starts from $-2$ and goes to the **left**. This indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **less than** $-2.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-372bfce3-55de-5261-b54b-bd57baebf86e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-372bfce3-55de-5261-b54b-bd57baebf86e" :answer-field/id #uuid "372bfce3-55de-5261-b54b-bd57baebf86e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a98fc996-0d00-5ba4-ac4b-c42bb0f40474" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a98fc996-0d00-5ba4-ac4b-c42bb0f40474" "answer-12bb050c-17f2-5b49-bd67-5399140422df" "answer-73428768-362c-5264-a417-4dc542a945aa" "answer-3071d7a4-198e-5069-8278-a358ecc1769d" "answer-96b99f5f-b2db-5301-a474-08090ce19f3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a98fc996-0d00-5ba4-ac4b-c42bb0f40474" :answer/id #uuid "a98fc996-0d00-5ba4-ac4b-c42bb0f40474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12bb050c-17f2-5b49-bd67-5399140422df" :answer/id #uuid "12bb050c-17f2-5b49-bd67-5399140422df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73428768-362c-5264-a417-4dc542a945aa" :answer/id #uuid "73428768-362c-5264-a417-4dc542a945aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3071d7a4-198e-5069-8278-a358ecc1769d" :answer/id #uuid "3071d7a4-198e-5069-8278-a358ecc1769d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96b99f5f-b2db-5301-a474-08090ce19f3b" :answer/id #uuid "96b99f5f-b2db-5301-a474-08090ce19f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le -2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d83cabb0-45f8-5769-8a35-16968ddc61ef" :question/id #uuid "d83cabb0-45f8-5769-8a35-16968ddc61ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-63242" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c334d2f47b36ac6d7ca620e044afda648aafa13ad9559af5131a50d2768d439.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "There is an **open** circle at $x=\\frac{3}{4},$ and the red arrow starts from $\\frac{3}{4}$ and goes to the **left**. This indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **less than ** $\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<\\frac{3}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d71b73e1-4a7b-508f-bb0f-fc541b67f4d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d71b73e1-4a7b-508f-bb0f-fc541b67f4d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "d71b73e1-4a7b-508f-bb0f-fc541b67f4d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16699bc6-4cf2-5912-8eaf-e9ee4f6a2780" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18b678d2-a4f4-5e77-8478-b569611a3a64" "answer-dc058d6a-3e48-53d4-8b1c-58f26a1450af" "answer-16699bc6-4cf2-5912-8eaf-e9ee4f6a2780" "answer-8b6e935c-04e8-51e3-8cc2-3bccda178608" "answer-38a5ae54-1f74-5301-8bd3-5f5e19195489"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18b678d2-a4f4-5e77-8478-b569611a3a64" :answer/id #uuid "18b678d2-a4f4-5e77-8478-b569611a3a64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc058d6a-3e48-53d4-8b1c-58f26a1450af" :answer/id #uuid "dc058d6a-3e48-53d4-8b1c-58f26a1450af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16699bc6-4cf2-5912-8eaf-e9ee4f6a2780" :answer/id #uuid "16699bc6-4cf2-5912-8eaf-e9ee4f6a2780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x<\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b6e935c-04e8-51e3-8cc2-3bccda178608" :answer/id #uuid "8b6e935c-04e8-51e3-8cc2-3bccda178608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38a5ae54-1f74-5301-8bd3-5f5e19195489" :answer/id #uuid "38a5ae54-1f74-5301-8bd3-5f5e19195489" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x>\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060988 :tutorial/content "An **inequality** is a mathematical statement that represents a set of numbers on the number line. For example, the set of numbers that are greater than or equal to $0$ can also be represented by the inequality\n\n$$\nx \\; {\\color{red}\\geq} \\; 0\n$$\n\nHere, the sign ${\\color{red}\\geq}$ means \"greater than or equal to.\" So the above statement in words is \"$x$ is greater than or equal to zero.\" For example,\n\n- the numbers $0,$ $1,$ and $7.321$ all satisfy the inequality, while\n\n- the numbers $-0.01,$ $-8,$ and $-123$ do not.\n\nWe can represent this inequality visually using a number line. To do so, we first plot the number zero as a red dot on the number line. The rest of the numbers that are greater than or equal to $0$ lie to the right of $0,$ so we represent them using a red line that extends to the right of $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/b6/b6e9b825a43d1305fc151797351319d1e8f53f7d0dec24a10096a91bc4482855.png)\n\nIn general, there are four types of inequalities:\n\n$\\ge\\quad$ *greater than or equal* - this is represented by a filled circle $\\Large\\color{red}\\bullet$ and an arrow that goes to the right $\\Large\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\rightarrow}$\n\n$>\\quad$ *greater than* - this is represented by an empty circle $\\Large\\color{red}\\circ$ and an arrow that goes to the right $\\Large\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\rightarrow}$\n\n$\\le\\quad$ *less than or equal* - this is represented by a filled circle $\\Large\\color{red}\\bullet$ and an arrow that goes to the left $\\Large\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\leftarrow}$\n\n$<\\quad$ *less than* - this is represented by an empty circle $\\Large\\color{red}\\circ$  and an arrow that goes to the left $\\Large\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\leftarrow}$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059901 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
